    ("sudoers NOPASSWD", "`user ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl restart app` grants one command passwordless; `visudo -c` validates syntax (a broken sudoers bricks admin access). Prefer command-scoped grants over ALL."),
    ("capabilities bounding", "`capsh --print` shows effective sets; grant singly (`--cap-add NET_BIND_SERVICE`) instead of privileged. Capabilities partition root's powers — learn the 40 names and containers stop needing `--privileged`."),
    ("unshare namespaces demo", "`unshare --pid --fork --mount-proc bash` spawns a PID-1 shell in fresh namespaces — containers demystified in one command. Add `--net` for isolated networking (needs veth setup) and `--user` for mapped UIDs."),
    ("oom_score_adj tuning", "Tune `/proc/PID/oom_score_adj` (-1000 immune, +1000 first victim) so expendable workers die before databases. Container `--oom-score-adj` maps here; `--oom-kill-disable` risks host lockups instead of one death."),
    ("coredump analysis", "`coredumpctl list` finds crashes, `coredumpctl debug PID` opens gdb with the core; `ulimit -c unlimited` plus `kernel.core_pattern` must allow dumps first. Cores contain secrets — restrict directory permissions."),
    ("sysctl runtime tune", "`sysctl -w net.ipv4.ip_forward=1` applies live; persist in `/etc/sysctl.d/*.conf` — reboot wipes runtime-only tuning silently."),
    ("sysctl vm swappiness", "`vm.swappiness` (0-100) biases reclaim toward caches vs swap; databases want low values, batch boxes tolerate higher."),
    ("ulimit nofile raise", "`ulimit -n 65535` raises shell FD limits; systemd `LimitNOFILE=` and `/etc/security/limits.conf` persist for services/logins."),
    ("nice renice ionice", "`nice -n 10` deprioritizes batch CPU; `renice` adjusts live; `ionice -c3` idles disk hogs — noisy neighbors tamed without kills."),
    ("cgroups v1 layout", "Legacy v1 splits controllers (`/sys/fs/cgroup/cpu,memory`) per hierarchy; v2 unifies — know which your distro/tools expect."),
    ("systemd-run scope", "`systemd-run --scope` wraps ad-hoc commands in cgroups with limits/accounting — one-off resource control without unit files."),
    ("loginctl sessions", "`loginctl list-sessions` + `show-session` audit logins graphically and remotely; lingering sessions hold resources and mounts."),
    ("faillock deny", "`faillock` tallies auth failures (deny after N); unlock with `--user x --reset` — brute-force defense with self-lockout risk."),
    ("chage password aging", "`chage -M 90 user` enforces rotation; `-l` audits expiry before lockouts surprise on-call rotations."),
    ("lastlog wtmp", "`lastlog` shows every user's latest login (stale accounts stand out); `last -x` adds shutdown/runlevel history."),
    ("sosreport support", "`sosreport` bundles logs/configs for vendor tickets; `--clean` obfuscates IPs/hostnames before uploading."),
    ("tuned profiles", "`tuned-adm profile latency-performance|virtual-guest` applies workload presets (scheduler, disk, network knobs) in one switch."),
    ("irqbalance numa", "`irqbalance` spreads device interrupts across CPUs/NUMA nodes; database/network boxes verify placement with `numastat`."),
    ("kdump crash kernel", "`kdump` boots a capture kernel on panic for vmcore analysis; test with `echo c > /proc/sysrq-trigger` in maintenance windows only."),
