    ("list index start", "`.index(x, mula)` searches from offset (repeated finds advance the start) — ValueError means absent, catch it."),
    ("nested list trap", "`[[0]*3]*3` shares ONE inner row (mutating [0][0] hits all rows!); `[[0]*3 for _ in range(3)]` builds independent rows."),
    ("slice assignment", "`a[1:3] = [9]` replaces spans (length may change); `a[1:1] = [x]` inserts without append — slices as editable windows."),
    ("del slice", "`del a[2:]` drops tails in place; `a = a[:2]` rebinds (aliases keep old) — in-place vs rebind matters with shared refs."),
    ("tuple single syntax", "`(1,)` is a 1-tuple; `(1)` is just int — trailing comma makes tuples, not parentheses."),
    ("namedtuple", "`Titik = namedtuple('Titik', 'x y')` gives tuple memory with named fields (immutable records, `_asdict()` for JSON)."),
    ("tuple unpack nested", "`(nama, (bandar, poskod)) = rekod` unpacks nested shapes positionally — CSV/API rows in one line."),
    ("dict views live", "`.keys()/.values()/.items()` are LIVE views (reflect later mutations); `list(d)` snapshots — iterate `list()` when deleting mid-loop."),
    ("dict fromkeys trap", "`dict.fromkeys(kunci, [])` shares ONE list across keys; comprehension `{k: [] for k in kunci}` isolates — same aliasing trap as nested lists."),
    ("zip to dict", "`dict(zip(kunci, nilai))` pairs parallel lists; `zip(..., strict=True)` (3.10+) aborts on length drift instead of silent truncation."),
    ("dict missing key", "`collections.defaultdict` / `__missing__` auto-create; `setdefault` one-offs; `try/except KeyError` for genuinely exceptional absence."),
    ("dict order guarantee", "Dicts keep insertion order (3.7+ language guarantee); `OrderedDict` only for move-to-end/reorder APIs now."),
    ("sort dict by value", "`sorted(d.items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1])` ranks by value; `dict(...)` rebuilds ordered — Counter.most_common shortcuts frequencies."),
    ("invert dict", "`{v: k for k, v in d.items()}` inverts (later wins on dupes) — non-unique values need grouping (defaultdict(list)), not inversion."),
    ("set literal trap", "`{}` is an empty DICT; `set()` is the empty set — braces with items make sets, bare braces make dicts."),
    ("discard vs remove", "`.discard(x)` never raises (idempotent deletes); `.remove(x)` raises on absence — membership-unknown code uses discard."),
    ("set algebra", "`a | b` union, `&` intersect, `-` difference, `^` symmetric-difference return new sets; `|=`/`&=` update in place."),
    ("frozenset keys", "`frozenset` (immutable, hashable) serves as dict keys/set members — tag-combos and cache keys without tuples."),
    ("dedupe preserve order", "`list(dict.fromkeys(item))` dedupes order-preserving (hashables); unhashables need manual seen-lists — set() alone scrambles order."),
    ("class vs instance attrs", "Attributes set on `self` are per-instance; on the class shared (mutable class attrs leak across instances!) — defaults live on class, state on self."),
    ("classmethod factories", "`@classmethod def dari_csv(cls, path)` constructs via the actual subclass — alternative constructors that inherit correctly."),
    ("staticmethod utils", "`@staticmethod` namespaces pure helpers needing neither self nor cls — namespaced functions, not methods."),
    ("property setter", "`@property` + `@x.setter` compute/validate attribute access (`obj.harga = -1` can raise) — public attribute feel, private control."),
    ("str vs repr dunder", "`__str__` for users (readable), `__repr__` for developers (unambiguous, ideally re-creatable) — define repr always, str when displayed."),
    ("len getitem contains", "`__len__`, `__getitem__`, `__contains__` make custom collections work with `len()`, `[]`, `in` and even iteration — protocol over inheritance."),
    ("callable instances", "`def __call__(self, x):` makes instances invocable (`model(x)`) — stateful functions and handlers without closures."),
    ("enter exit protocol", "`__enter__` acquires, `__exit__(exc_type, ...)` releases (return True only to suppress!) — files, locks, transactions all share this shape."),
    ("iter next protocol", "`__iter__` returns the iterator, `__next__` raises StopIteration at exhaustion — `for` works on anything implementing both."),
    ("inheritance mro", "`Kelas.__mro__` shows method resolution order (C3 linearization); `super()` follows it — diamonds resolve deterministically, print MRO when confused."),
    ("abc abstractmethod", "`class B(ABC)` + `@abstractmethod` blocks instantiation until subclasses implement — contracts the interpreter enforces."),
    ("dataclass field factory", "`field(default_factory=list)` gives per-instance mutables (never bare `[]`); `__post_init__` validates derived state after construction."),
    ("dataclass frozen kwonly", "`@dataclass(frozen=True, kw_only=True)` (3.10+ kw_only) builds immutable, explicit value objects — hashable config records."),
    ("dataclass asdict replace", "`asdict()` deep-converts to dicts (JSON-ready); `replace(obj, x=1)` clones with changes — immutable-style updates."),
    ("enum flag auto", "`class Kebenaran(Flag)` bit-combines (`R | W`); `auto()` values, `@unique` guards dupes — named constants with iteration."),
    ("name mangling", "`self.__rahsia` mangles to `_Kelas__rahsia` (subclass-collision guard, not security) — single `_` is the real 'private' convention."),
    ("total_ordering", "`@total_ordering` + `__eq__` + one of `__lt__` derives all comparisons — ranking classes without four near-identical methods."),
    ("getattr fallback", "`def __getattr__(self, nama):` fires only when normal lookup fails (lazy attrs, proxies) — `__getattribute__` intercepts everything (recursion trap!)."),
    ("descriptors protocol", "`__get__/__set__/__delete__` on a class attribute build managed fields (ORM columns, validators) — property is one instance of this."),
    ("init_subclass hook", "`def __init_subclass__(cls, nama=None):` registers plugins/validates subclasses at definition — registries without metaclasses."),
    ("copy vs deepcopy objects", "`copy.copy` shares nested (shallow), `copy.deepcopy` clones the graph (`__deepcopy__` customizes) — graphs/cycles need the latter."),
    ("composition over inheritance", "Hold collaborators (`self.enjin = Enjin()`) instead of deep hierarchies — behavior composes, MRO stays flat, tests inject fakes."),
    ("functools wraps", "`@wraps(f)` copies name/docstring to wrappers — undecorated metadata breaks help(), logging and debuggers."),
    ("parameterized decorators", "Decorators with args need THREE levels (`outer(args) → decorator → wrapper`) — factories returning decorators, plain and simple."),
    ("decorator stacking order", "`@a @b def f` applies b first (bottom-up), executes a's wrapper outermost — read stacks bottom-first."),
    ("cached_property", "`@cached_property` computes once then caches as attribute (no-arg methods, instance dict) — expensive derivations without __init__ cost."),
    ("singledispatch", "`@singledispatch` + `.register(type)` overloads by first-arg type (JSON serializers, renderers) — open extension without if-chains."),
    ("operator itemgetter sorted", "`sorted(pengguna, key=operator.itemgetter('umur'))` beats lambdas in speed and picklability — attrgetter/methodcaller for attrs/methods."),
    ("recursion limit", "`sys.getrecursionlimit()` (~1000); deep recursion overflows — rewrite as loops/stacks or `setrecursionlimit` deliberately (never blindly)."),
    ("map filter vs comprehensions", "`map(f, xs)`/`filter(ok, xs)` are lazy iterators (compose without temp lists); comprehensions read better — both beat manual append loops."),
    ("iter sentinel", "`iter(fail.read, '')` calls a zero-arg function until sentinel — chunked reads without while-True."),
    ("next default", "`next(gen, None)` returns the default instead of raising StopIteration — first-match searches in one line."),
    ("yield from delegate", "`yield from sub()` streams sub-generators (and forwards send/throw) — recursive walks read flat, values propagate."),
    ("itertools product", "`product('AB', repeat=2)` cartesian-joins (test matrices, grids); `permutations` orders, `combinations` subsets — counting without nesting."),
    ("itertools groupby sorted", "`groupby(sorted(data, key=k), key=k)` groups CONSECUTIVE equals (sort first!) — SQL GROUP BY semantics in memory."),
    ("itertools infinite", "`count()`, `cycle()`, `repeat()` never end — always pair with `islice`/takewhile/break or loops hang forever."),
    ("itertools accumulate", "`accumulate(sales)` running totals; `initial=` seeds; `zip_longest(fillvalue=0)` pairs ragged rows without truncation."),
    ("pairwise batched", "`pairwise()` (3.10+) yields overlaps (`(a,b),(b,c)`) for diffs; `batched(n)` (3.12+) chunks strictly — sliding windows, no indexing."),
    ("multiple context managers", "`with open(a) as f, open(b, 'w') as g:` stacks managers (or parenthesized multi-line) — one indent, many resources, all closed."),
    ("contextmanager decorator", "`@contextmanager` turns try/yield/finally generators into `with` blocks (timers, temp states) — yield separates setup from teardown."),
    ("ExitStack dynamic", "`with ExitStack() as s:` registers N runtime-known cleanups (`enter_context`, `callback`) — dynamic file sets close correctly."),
    ("open exclusive x", "`open('baru.txt', 'x')` fails if exists (no clobber races); `r+`/`w+`/`a+` add read/write to each base mode."),
    ("file iteration memory", "`for baris in fail:` streams line by line (constant memory); `.read().splitlines()` loads all — gigabyte logs demand iteration."),
    ("seek tell binary", "`.seek(0)` rewinds, `.tell()` reports offsets (logs/checkpoints); text-mode seeks need opaque cookies from tell(), not arithmetic."),
    ("pathlib read write", "`Path('a.txt').read_text(encoding='utf-8')` / `.write_text(...)` one-line small files — no manual open/close."),
    ("pathlib parts", "`.name/.stem/.suffix/.parent/.parts` dissect paths without string surgery; `/` joins portably — splitext logic built in."),
    ("pathlib glob rglob", "`Path('.').rglob('*.py')` recursive finds; `.glob('*.md')` shallow — pathlib-native search without os.walk."),
    ("pathlib mkdir rename", "`.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)` nests safely; `.rename()`/`.replace()` move (replace overwrites) — return values are new Paths."),
    ("path resolve home", "`.resolve()` absolutizes + dereferences symlinks; `Path.home()` / `Path.cwd()` anchor portably — never hardcode `/home/x`."),
    ("os walk topdown", "`os.walk()` yields (dir, subdirs, files) top-down (prune by editing subdirs in place); `os.scandir()` entries carry cached stat — fast trees."),
    ("os environ getenv", "`os.environ['WAJIB']` raises when missing (fail-fast configs); `os.getenv('PILIHAN', 'lalai')` defaults — secrets via env, never code."),
    ("shutil operations", "`shutil.copytree/rmtree/move/copy2` (copy2 keeps metadata); `shutil.which('ffmpeg')` locates binaries; `disk_usage('/')` capacities — shell file ops in Python."),
    ("glob recursive", "`glob('**/*.log', recursive=True)` deep-matches; `iglob` streams huge trees — `**` needs the flag, else it's one level."),
    ("tempfile cleanup", "`TemporaryFile()` auto-deletes on close; `mkdtemp()` + try/finally rmtree for dirs — predictable /tmp names invite symlink attacks."),
    ("csv dictreader", "`csv.DictReader(f)` yields named rows (header-driven); `writer(f, quoting=QUOTE_MINIMAL)` escapes commas/newlines — never hand-split CSV."),
    ("pickle warning", "`pickle.load` executes embedded code — NEVER unpickle untrusted input (use JSON); `protocol=HIGHEST_PROTOCOL` for own caches."),
    ("struct pack", "`struct.pack('>HI', ver, saiz)` builds binary protocols (endianness prefix!); `calcsize` sizes buffers — sockets/files interop."),
    ("sqlite parameterized", "`cur.execute('SELECT * FROM t WHERE id=?', (i,))` — `?` placeholders (never f-strings: injection!); `executemany` bulk-inserts, commit explicitly."),
    ("sqlite row_factory", "`con.row_factory = sqlite3.Row` enables `baris['nama']` dict-style access; `total_changes` audits writes per connection."),
    ("configparser sections", "`configparser.ConfigParser()` `.read('app.ini')`, `getboolean('s', 'debug')` typed getters — INI without manual parsing."),
    ("re search vs match", "`re.search` scans anywhere, `re.match` anchors at start (use `fullmatch` for entire-string validation) — most 'broken regex' is match-vs-search confusion."),
    ("re groups named", "`m = re.search(r'(?P<tahun>\\\\d{4})-(?P<bulan>\\\\d{2})', s); m.group('tahun')` names captures (logs, dates) — reorder-proof versus $1."),
    ("re sub function", "`re.sub(r'\\\\d+', lambda m: f'[{m.group()}]', s)` computes replacements (redaction, templating) — backrefs `\\\\1` for plain swaps."),
    ("re split keep", "`re.split(r'(,|;)', s)` keeps delimiters via groups (tokenizers); `maxsplit=1` mirrors partition for regex."),
    ("re flags", "`re.IGNORECASE` (case), `re.MULTILINE` (^$ per line), `re.VERBOSE` (commented patterns) — flags fix whole bug classes, not single matches."),
    ("greedy vs lazy", "`<.+>` gobbles to the LAST `>` (greedy); `<.+?>` stops at the first (lazy) — tag parsing needs lazy or negated classes."),
    ("shlex split quote", "`shlex.split('a \"b c\"')` parses shell-like syntax honoring quotes; `shlex.join()` (3.8+) rebuilds safely — commands as data, not strings."),
    ("difflib suggestions", "`difflib.get_close_matches(input, pilihan, n=3, cutoff=0.6)` powers 'did you mean?' (CLI typos, search) — SequenceMatcher.ratio() scores pairs."),
    ("textwrap dedent", "`textwrap.dedent('''...''')` strips code indentation from embedded SQL/templates — indented source, clean strings."),
    ("unicode normalize", "`unicodedata.normalize('NFC', s)` unifies composed vs decomposed forms before comparing user text — Malay/Jawi input needs this."),
    ("datetime aware now", "`datetime.now(timezone.utc)` aware timestamps (utcnow() is deprecated!) — naive vs aware never compare; store UTC, display zoned."),
    ("datetime iso parse", "`.isoformat()` serializes (`2026-10-12T...`), `datetime.fromisoformat(s)` parses back — JSON APIs without format-string fragility."),
    ("strptime codes", "`datetime.strptime('12/10/2026', '%d/%m/%Y')` parses with `%Y %m %d %H %M %S` codes — mismatched codes raise, never guess."),
    ("timedelta arithmetic", "`tarikh + timedelta(hari=7)` shifts dates (weeks/minutes kwargs); subtraction yields timedeltas (`.days`, `.total_seconds()`) — expiry math without calendars."),
    ("zoneinfo", "`ZoneInfo('Asia/Kuala_Lumpur')` IANA zones from stdlib (3.9+) — `.astimezone(zone)` converts; pytz-style localize() is obsolete."),
    ("time monotonic", "`time.monotonic()` (uptime clock, never steps) for timeouts/benchmarks; `perf_counter()` highest resolution; `sleep()` yields the thread."),
    ("threading basics", "`Thread(target=kerja, args=(q,)).start()` parallels I/O (network, disk); CPU-bound threads serialize on the GIL — threads for waiting, processes for crunching."),
    ("threading Lock Event", "`Lock` serializes shared mutation (`with kunci:`); `Event.set()/wait()` signals readiness across threads — shared state needs one of these."),
    ("queue threadsafe", "`queue.Queue()` passes work between threads safely (`.put/.get/.task_done/.join`) — hand-rolled lists + sleeps race; queues don't."),
    ("gil explained", "The GIL allows one bytecode thread at a time (C extensions release it for I/O) — threading speeds downloads, multiprocessing speeds math."),
    ("futures as_completed", "`as_completed(futs)` yields futures in finish order (progress bars, first-result wins); `.map()` preserves submit order instead."),
    ("multiprocessing pool", "`Pool().map(f, data)` spreads CPU work across cores (picklable funcs only); `if __name__ == '__main__'` guard mandatory (spawn re-imports!)."),
    ("asyncio run gather", "`asyncio.run(main())` boots the loop once; `await asyncio.gather(a(), b())` parallels coroutines — one loop per program, never nest run()."),
    ("asyncio wait_for timeout", "`await asyncio.wait_for(fetch(), timeout=5)` bounds hangs (TimeoutError on expiry); 3.11+ `asyncio.timeout(5)` scopes blocks instead."),
    ("asyncio to_thread", "`await asyncio.to_thread(blocking_io)` offloads sync libraries (boto3, psycopg2) without freezing the loop — the sync/async bridge."),
    ("unittest testcase", "`class Ujian(unittest.TestCase)` + `assertEqual/assertRaises` + `setUp/tearDown` per test — stdlib suites with zero dependencies."),
    ("mock patch target", "`@patch('modul.Kelas')` (patch WHERE looked up, not defined!) with `MagicMock(return_value=...)`; `assert_called_with` verifies wiring — external services never hit in unit tests."),
    ("pytest parametrize", "`@pytest.mark.parametrize('a,b,j', [(1,2,3),(0,0,0)])` multiplies one test across cases — tables beat copy-pasted test functions."),
    ("pytest fixture approx", "`@pytest.fixture` builds fresh state per test (tmp files, app clients); `pytest.approx(0.1+0.2) == 0.3` compares floats honestly."),
    ("doctest format", "`>>> tambah(2, 3)` then `5` in docstrings doubles as tests (`pytest --doctest-modules`) — examples that CI verifies never rot."),
    ("pip show freeze", "`pip show requests` (version, location, requires); `pip freeze > requirements.txt` pins exact deploys — `list --outdated` flags drift."),
    ("pip uninstall download", "`pip uninstall -y pkg` removes cleanly; `pip download -d ./wheels -r req.txt` vendors for air-gapped installs."),
    ("venv prompt", "`python -m venv .venv --prompt projek` names the shell prompt (multi-project sanity); activate per shell, never commit the dir."),
    ("uv commands", "`uv venv && uv pip install -r req.txt` (Rust-fast resolver); `uv run skrip.py` auto-manages ephemeral envs — pip-compatible, order-of-magnitude faster."),
    ("poetry basics", "`poetry init/add/install/run pytest` manages env+lockfile together (`poetry.lock` committed); `poetry shell` activates — one tool, no manual venvs."),
    ("pipx tools", "`pipx install black` isolates CLI tools (each its own env, all on PATH); `pipx run pycowsay 'hi'` one-shots without installing."),
    ("conda basics", "`conda create -n projek python=3.12 && conda activate projek` (binary deps: numpy, CUDA) — heavier than venv, unmatched for scientific stacks."),
    ("importlib metadata version", "`importlib.metadata.version('requests')` reads installed versions at runtime (about-boxes, bug reports); `files()` lists package contents."),
    ("TYPE_CHECKING guard", "`if TYPE_CHECKING:` imports types only for checkers (zero runtime cost/cycles) — string annotations + this break every circular import."),
    ("union syntax pipe", "`def f(x: int | None)` (3.10+) beats `Optional[int]`; `int | str` beats `Union[]` — runtime-valid syntax, no typing imports."),
    ("TypeVar generics", "`T = TypeVar('T'); def pertama(xs: list[T]) -> T:` preserves element types through helpers — copy-paste `Any` erases them."),
    ("Final decorator", "`HAD: Final = 100` (and `@final` on classes/methods) tells checkers what must never rebind/override — constants with enforcement."),
    ("mypy strict", "`mypy --strict src/` (untyped defs, unchecked bodies flagged); fix incrementally (`--disallow-untyped-defs` first) — types as CI gate."),
    ("ruff check format", "`ruff check .` (lint, pyflakes+pycodestyle speed) + `ruff format .` (black-compatible) — one binary replaces flake8/isort/pyupgrade configs."),
    ("black line length", "`black -l 100 .` normalizes style project-wide; `--check` in CI diffs without writing — formatted diffs review logic, not whitespace."),
    ("pdb commands", "`breakpoint()` then `n`ext/`s`tep/`c`ontinue/`p x`/`l`ist/`w`here/`q`uit — `pp` pretty-prints; post-mortem via `pdb.pm()` after crashes."),
    ("secrets tokens", "`secrets.token_hex(16)` (CSPRNG) mints session tokens/reset links; `random` is predictable — secrets for security, random for games."),
    ("hashlib file hash", "`hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest()` fingerprints downloads (compare published sums!); chunked `.update()` hashes gigabytes streaming."),
    ("hmac compare", "`hmac.compare_digest(a, b)` constant-time secret comparison; `hmac.new(key, msg, sha256)` signs webhooks — `==` leaks via timing."),
    ("uuid versions", "`uuid.uuid4()` random ids (sessions, filenames); `uuid5(NAMESPACE_DNS, name)` deterministic (dedup keys) — strings via `str()`."),
    ("base64 urlsafe", "`base64.urlsafe_b64encode(b)` embeds binary in URLs/filenames (`-_` not `+/`); decode then compare_digest — never `==` on secrets."),
    ("heapq topn", "`heapq.nlargest(5, skor)` ranks without full sorts; `heappush/heappop` maintain live leaderboards — O(n log k), not O(n log n)."),
    ("bisect sorted insert", "`bisect.insort(senarai, x)` keeps sorted order on insert; `bisect_left` finds positions (rankings, schedules) — binary search, no scans."),
    ("copy deepcopy", "`copy.copy` shares nested objects (shallow); `copy.deepcopy` clones graphs (`__deepcopy__` customizes) — config templates need the latter."),
    ("pprint logs", "`pprint(data, width=100, depth=2)` renders nested structures readably in logs; `pformat` captures to strings for exceptions."),
    ("enum IntEnum", "`class Peranan(IntEnum)` compares with ints (DB codes, protocols); `auto()` values + `@unique` guard dupes."),
    ("timeit benchmark", "`python -m timeit -s '...' 'kod'` (or `timeit.repeat`) micro-benchmarks correctly (warmup, best-of) — `time.time()` diffs lie about noise."),
    ("logging basicConfig", "`logging.basicConfig(level=INFO, format='%(asctime)s %(name)s %(levelname)s %(message)s')` once at entry; per-module `getLogger(__name__)` inherits — prints can't filter."),
    ("logging exception", "`log.exception('simpan gagal')` inside except logs message + traceback automatically — the one-line incident record."),
    ("warnings warn", "`warnings.warn('lapuk', DeprecationWarning, stacklevel=2)` flags callers (not the library line!); `-W error` promotes to failures in tests."),
    ("platform info", "`platform.system()/machine()/python_version()` branches per OS/arch in bug reports and installers — `sys.platform` for quick checks."),
    ("argparse subparsers", "`add_subparsers(dest='cmd')` builds git-style CLIs (`alat tambah ...`); `nargs='+'` collects lists, `type=int` converts free."),
    ("requests post json", "`requests.post(url, json=data, timeout=10)` sends JSON (`Content-Type` auto); `raise_for_status()` turns HTTP errors into exceptions — never omit timeout."),
    ("requests session retry", "`Session()` pools connections (mount `HTTPAdapter(max_retries=3)`); Basic auth via `auth=(u, p)`, tokens via headers — one session per app, not per call."),
    ("urllib parse", "`urllib.parse.quote/query: urlencode({'q': 'kopi o'})/urljoin(base, path)` builds URLs safely — hand-concatenated `?a=b&c=` breaks on spaces and `&`."),
    ("http server handler", "`class H(BaseHTTPRequestHandler): def do_GET(self): ...` + `HTTPServer(('', 8000), H)` serves webhooks/mocks in stdlib — `python -m http.server` for static only."),
    ("socket basics", "`socket.create_connection((hos, 80), timeout=5)` connects; `bind/listen/accept` serve — `with` closes; real apps prefer frameworks over raw sockets."),
    ("flask route json", "`@app.post('/tambah')` + `request.get_json()` + `jsonify(...)`; `app.run(debug=True)` dev only — gunicorn/uvicorn serve production."),
    ("fastapi endpoint", "`@app.get('/barang/{id}')` with type hints validates automatically (422 on bad input); `TestClient(app)` tests without servers — docs at /docs free."),
    ("django orm basics", "`python manage.py migrate` applies schema; `Buku.objects.filter(harga__lt=50)` queries (lazy!); `createsuperuser` + admin gives instant backoffice."),
    ("pandas read head", "`pd.read_csv('j.csv')` → DataFrame; `.head()/.info()/.describe()` profile in 3 lines — `parse_dates=['tarikh']` fixes dtypes at load."),
    ("pandas groupby merge", "`.groupby('bandar')['jualan'].sum()` aggregates; `pd.merge(a, b, on='id', how='left')` joins — `to_csv(index=False)` exports cleanly."),
    ("numpy basics", "`np.arange(12).reshape(3, 4)` builds grids; `dtype=` controls memory; broadcasting aligns shapes (`(3,1)+(1,4)`) — vectorize, never Python-loop arrays."),
    ("matplotlib plot", "`plt.plot(x, y); plt.xlabel('...'); plt.savefig('carta.png')` (savefig before show!); `plt.subplots()` for multi-panel — scripts save, notebooks show."),
    ("pillow resize", "`Image.open('a.jpg').resize((800, 600)).save('kecil.jpg')` thumbnails in 3 calls; `.convert('RGB')` before JPEG (alpha crashes saves)."),
    ("openpyxl cells", "`wb = load_workbook('x.xlsx'); ws['B2'].value` reads; assign + `wb.save()` writes — pandas for bulk, openpyxl for formatting."),
    ("pypdf extract", "`PdfReader('f.pdf').pages[i].extract_text()` mines text (scanned PDFs need OCR — empty strings mean images, not text)."),
    ("rich console table", "`from rich import print; print('[bold red]Gagal[/]')` styles terminals; `Table` + `Progress` replace hand-rolled dashboards — logging stays plain."),
    ("tqdm progress", "`for x in tqdm(senaraian, desc='Proses'):` shows ETA bars (stderr, composable with logging); `total=` for generators — long loops narrate themselves."),
    ("click command", "`@click.command() @click.option('--n', default=1)` builds CLIs with `--help` free; `click.echo` (not print) respects piping/encoding."),
    ("typer run", "`def utama(nama: str): ...; typer.run(utama)` infers CLIs from type hints — click's power, function-signature brevity."),
    ("jinja2 template", "`Template('Helo {{ nama }}').render(nama='Ali')` (autoescape=True for HTML!); `{% for %}{% if %}` logic stays in templates, data in Python."),
    ("pyyaml safe", "`yaml.safe_load(f)` (NEVER bare load — code execution!); `safe_dump` writes — configs human-editable, CI-validated."),
    ("dotenv load", "`load_dotenv()` reads `.env` into environ (dev only, never commit); `os.getenv('KUNCI')` with explicit failure when required vars miss."),
    ("psycopg2 placeholders", "`cur.execute('SELECT * FROM t WHERE id = %s', (i,))` — `%s` placeholders (NOT f-strings: injection!); `RealDictCursor` returns named rows."),
